Hi [REDACTED_NAME],

I came across your profile and your background really stood out to me,
especially your 13+ years of experience in detection engineering, threat
research, SIEM engineering, threat hunting, and translating MITRE ATT&CK
techniques into production-ready detections. Your work across CrowdStrike
Falcon, Microsoft Sentinel, Carbon Black, Sumo Logic Cloud SIEM, and your
experience building scalable detection capabilities is particularly
impressive.

I work as a Reverse Recruiter, meaning I work directly for job seekers
instead of companies. My role is to help professionals identify strong-fit
opportunities, connect with hiring managers and recruiters, and improve
their visibility throughout the hiring process rather than relying only on
traditional online applications.

I also help support the full application process strategically, including
positioning, outreach, and application foundation tools designed to
strengthen a candidate's chances of getting noticed.

I recently came across a Senior Detection Engineer / Threat Research
opportunity with a growing organization offering approximately $150K=E2=80=93$190K
total compensation with remote/hybrid flexibility. Based on your experience
building behavioral detections, threat intelligence integrations, SIEM
engineering, detection tuning, and adversary focused research, I believe
you could be an excellent fit.

The role focuses on detection engineering, threat research, SIEM
optimization, threat hunting, MITRE ATT&CK mapping, and collaborating with
security operations teams to strengthen enterprise cyber defense areas that
closely align with your expertise.

Would you be open to hearing more about it?

Best Regards,
*MASHOOD SEKINAT *
